course: dictionary
lesson: 169
title: Aggressive: angry, forceful or fast
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Aggressive has more than one meaning, so the context tells you which one is right. The main meaning is angry and ready to attack, fight or hurt others. «Training with shouting, smacking or fear can make dogs scared or aggressive, so modern trainers use rewards because they work better and are kind.» Here aggressive means a dog that is ready to bite or attack, which is what the fear and shouting lead to.
explain: Aggressive can also describe someone who is very determined and forceful, like an aggressive player in a game who attacks the ball a lot. Look at the words around it to decide. Shouting and pushing are aggressive in a bad way, but a sports player who plays hard and fast is aggressive in a fair, strong way.
explain: In medicine, an aggressive illness spreads fast. So if a doctor calls an illness aggressive, she means it is spreading quickly, not that the illness is angry. Always ask: does the sentence describe a feeling, a way of playing, or speed?
fact: Aggressive means angry and ready to attack, fight or hurt others.
fact: «Aggressive» can also mean very determined and forceful, as in an aggressive player in a game.
fact: In medicine, an aggressive illness spreads fast.
fact: Synonyms for angry aggressive are hostile and violent; these are strong words, so use them only when the sentence is serious.
fact: «Keep your distance and never feed wild animals»: an animal that gets used to human food loses its fear of people and may get aggressive.
exercise: «Training with shouting, smacking or fear can make dogs scared or aggressive.» What does aggressive mean here? | Very tired and sleepy | Happy to play | *Ready to attack or hurt | Quiet and shy
exercise: In a game, what does an aggressive player do? | Sits on the bench all match | Hides from the ball | *Attacks a lot and plays very hard | Stops to rest often
exercise: «An animal that gets used to human food may get aggressive.» Why do the two golden rules say never feed wild animals? | Wild animals cannot eat human food | Animals like to be fed by children | *Fed animals lose their fear and may become aggressive | Food makes animals grow too big to move
test: A doctor says the illness is aggressive. What does that mean? | *It spreads fast | It goes away when you sleep | It is very quiet and slow | It only affects animals
test: Someone is shouting and pushing you. What should you do? | Stand still and wait for them to stop | Shout louder than them | Push back as hard as you can | *Stay calm, keep your distance and get help from an adult
exam: Which word is closest in meaning to aggressive when it means angry and ready to attack? | *Hostile | Gentle | Sleepy | Careful
